2. Basic Stack Operations
Operation                                                               Description
push(x)                                                         Inserts element x at the top.
pop()                                                           Removes and returns the top element.
peek() / top()                                                  Returns the top element without removing it.
isEmpty()                                                       Checks whether the stack is empty.
isFull()                                                        Checks whether an array-based stack is full.
size()                                                          Returns the number of elements.
display()                                                       Displays the stack elements.

Stack Overflow and Stack Underflow

• Stack Overflow: Occurs when an element is pushed into a full, fixed-capacity stack.
• Stack Underflow: Occurs when an element is popped from an empty stack.

Example: If an array-based stack has a capacity of 3 and already contains [10, 20, 30], pushing 40
causes overflow. Popping from an empty stack causes underflow.